Session 2 summary — criteria NOT yet met; substantial diagnostic progress with the root cause now cornered:

**Main finding (RULE-4 chain):** cache_coherency@32 fails 0/32 with the tenure floor ON (default) and effectively passes with it OFF (3020/3021) on clean substrate. The failure mechanism is a per-run set of 1-3 **victim nodes whose mounts go EIO-dead mid-test**: the tenure dwork release runs the inode-cluster destage on a shortform parent dir (ino 131, and even root ino 128), and `xfs_imap_to_bp` returns **-EIO for 1500 consecutive laps** (proven by new lap counters, with 3 nodes wedging on the same inode in the same second) — with no SCSI errors, no verifier failures, and no shutdown message. Build **6CFAB18E** (built, not yet run) adds the decisive discriminator probe: mid-loop plain-bdev read + shutdown-flag check, which will split device-failure vs buffer-layer-refusal vs silent-shutdown on the next run.

**Also this session:** repaired major test-infra rot that was fabricating failures — victim nodes' 6.1G root disks were 100% full from triplicated kernel logging (hygiene script deployed, rsyslog masked, journald capped); serial-console panic capture enabled on all 32 VMs; run.sh prep power-cycling parallelized (was ~40s/node serial); and a grub-file mangling incident from the ssh wrapper's arg flattening was diagnosed and fully repaired. Refuted along the way: slot-table ghosts, PR-key loss as current blocker, the sess-1 strand (its strike escalation now works), and the panic-as-driver theory.

**Next session:** run 6CFAB18E, read `P9-ICD-MIDLOOP`, root-fix the victim-death, then re-run the trio, dir_reuse@16/@32, and the full 1/2/4/8/16/32 ladder on the final build before writing the criteria marker.

